# The Road — Car Survival Game

## Stack

- HTML + vanilla JavaScript (no frameworks, no bundlers, no npm runtime)
- Single `index.html` with inline `<script>` for game logic
- Separate JS files: `constants.js`, `world.js`, `particles.js`, `audio.js`
- CSS in `ui.css`
- Procedurally generated infinite world with a single highway road

## Architecture

### World system (`world.js`)

The world is procedurally generated using seeded noise. A single highway road winds gently through biomes (temperate, cold, arid). Terrain is generated in 32x32-tile chunks loaded/unloaded around the player.

- `initWorld(seed)` — initialize with a seed
- `getWorldTerrainType(tileX, tileY)` — O(1) terrain lookup from cached chunks
- `updateWorldChunks(playerX, playerY, collectedSet)` — load nearby chunks, unload far ones
- `getRoadCenterX(tileY)` — road position at any Y coordinate

Structures (gas stations, diners, scrapyards) are placed at intervals along the road with entities (barrels, scrap, circuits, abandoned cars). Trees and rocks scatter naturally in appropriate terrain.

Interactive entities are stored in `gameState.entities` (a `Map` keyed by `"tileX,tileY"`). Collected entities are tracked in `gameState.collectedTiles` so they don't respawn when chunks reload.

### Rendering

`drawTerrain()` computes the visible tile range from the viewport and only iterates tiles on screen. Water tiles get animated wave effects. Texture images are drawn when available, falling back to `TERRAIN_COLORS`. A noise overlay adds visual variety.

### World coordinates

- World center is `(0, 0)`, car starts there on the road
- Tile `(tx, ty)` center is at world position `(tx * 80, ty * 80)`
- `TILE_SIZE = 80` world units per tile (defined in `world.js`)

### Key helper functions (global scope in index.html)

- `worldToTile(worldX, worldY)` → `[tileX, tileY]`
- `getTerrainTypeAtTile(tileX, tileY)` → terrain type string
- `getTerrainAt(worldX, worldY)` → terrain type string
- `getNearbyEntities(worldX, worldY, tileRadius)` → entity array

## Adding new terrain types

1. Add a display color in `constants.js` → `TERRAIN_COLORS`
2. Add generation logic in `world.js` → `getProceduralTerrainType()`
3. If interactive (collectible/obstacle), add the type to `ENTITY_TYPES` in `index.html`

## Adding new structures

1. Add a template to `STRUCTURE_TEMPLATES` in `world.js` with tile layout and entity spawns
2. Multiple variants per type are supported — just add more entries with the same weight distribution

## Files

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `index.html` | Main game (canvas, game loop, physics, UI) |
| `world.js` | Procedural world generation (noise, road, chunks, structures) |
| `constants.js` | Terrain colors, texture configs |
| `particles.js` | Exhaust, handbrake smoke, fire, water splash particles |
| `audio.js` | Sound manager using HTMLAudioElement |
| `ui.css` | Sidebar, status bars, minimap styling |
| `tools/editor-map-colors.php` | Standalone color replacement tool for map PNGs |

## Conventions

- No build step — open `index.html` directly or serve statically
- No npm packages at runtime (audio uses `new Audio()`, not Web Audio fetch)
- Keep all game logic in vanilla JS, no TypeScript
- Pixel art style: `image-rendering: pixelated` for map/minimap
